#Genomes, place in resources/genomes/
^g	test_genome.fa

#Features to annotate, place in resources/features/
#^f	bed file	n_windows	window_size
^f	g4Discovery.bed	1000	10

#Mean bedgraph window sizes
^a	1000

#Density bedgraph Window size
^w	1000000
^w	10000

#Significance threshold level, 0 is all data (no threshold),  1 is p <= 0.05,  2 is p <= 0.01,  3 is p <= 0.001,  4 is p <= 0.0001.
#Multiple levels can be specified (one per line). Density files are not produced for level 0.
^s	2

#Relationships between files
# Treatment and control fields are absolute (or relative) paths to the input file or directory.
# For FASTQ/BAM: provide the path to the file.
# For pod5: provide the path to the pod5 directory (searched recursively for .pod5 files).
# The raw_sample name is derived from the path basename minus extension.
#^    Sample          Treatment                                        Control
^r	Hsap_HG002_LCL	/path/to/reads/Hsap_HG002_LCL_Mn04.bam	/path/to/reads/Hsap_HG002_LCL_CTRL.bam

# Pod5 example:
#^r	Hsap_HG002_LCL	/sequencer/output/run_Mn04/pod5_pass	/sequencer/output/run_CTRL/pod5_pass

#Relationships whose inputs are ALREADY Uncalled4-aligned (nanoprint preprocess output).
# Same three fields as ^r. The DAG starts after signal alignment: no basecalling,
# no mapping, no filtering, no uncalled4 align. Keep the .bai next to each BAM.
# Do not put these BAMs on an ^r line — they would be re-mapped and lose their DTW tags.
#^    Sample          Treatment                          Control
#^u	Hsap_HG002_LCL	/path/to/Mn04_uncalled4.bam	/path/to/CTRL_uncalled4.bam

# Temporary intermediate files (deleted after downstream rules complete)
# Remove these lines to keep all intermediate files
^t	data/aligned_reads
# The Uncalled4 DTW TSVs are one row per aligned base per read - by far the
# largest thing the workflow writes. Marked temporary, each is deleted as soon
# as perbase_signal_deviation has consumed it.
^t	data/uncalled4_tsv
^t	data/bg
^t	data/bw
^t	data/windows
^t	data/annotations
^t	data/annotations_merged

#Other settings
^igv-bam
^igv-bigwig

# Direct modification calling by sample comparison (phases 2c/3c).
# Each read is tested base by base against a k-mer signal model built from the
# relationship's control; the track is the fraction of reads called modified.
# One line per backend; both may be given.
#   uncalled4   signal level from the Uncalled4 BAM (any sample with pod5 or ^u)
#   remora      signal level from pod5 via the Remora API (pip install ont-remora).
#               Needs raw signal: the ^r pod5 path, or a ^pod5 line for a ^u sample.
#^mod-calls	uncalled4
#^mod-calls	remora
# Raw signal for a ^u sample (remora backend): raw_sample name, pod5 file or directory.
#^pod5	Mn04_uncalled4	/sequencer/output/run_Mn04/pod5_pass
#^pod5	CTRL_uncalled4	/sequencer/output/run_CTRL/pod5_pass
# K-mer level table for Remora's signal mapping refinement. REQUIRED with
# '^mod-calls remora' - CONFIG.sh stops without it, because unrefined Remora levels
# are too noisy to use. Get it with:
#   git clone https://github.com/nanoporetech/kmer_models.git
#^remora-levels	/path/to/kmer_models/dna_r10.4.1_e8.2_400bps/9mer_levels_v1.txt
# Pooled control model: a name, then two or more raw_sample names (controls). Built
# in addition to each relationship's own (matched) control model, for every
# relationship whose control is a member. Comparing the two is the sample-to-sample
# reproducibility of the canonical signal.
#^mod-pool	G4_0mM_pool	CTRL_rep1_uncalled4	CTRL_rep2_uncalled4	CTRL_js4001_uncalled4
# Calling threshold, as --config keys (either or both; comma-separated lists allowed):
#   mod_pval=0.02   p-value below this (the default)
#   mod_fpr=0.02    the cutoff this fraction of the held-out control exceeds
# Outputs are kept apart by threshold: data/mod_reactivity/<backend>/<genome>/p0.02/...
# and .../fpr0.02/..., then matched/ or <pool name>/.
# To compare many settings side by side (filter, model and test options), see
# workflow/sweeps/mod_sweep.smk and its example table.
# Other --config keys: mod_mad (15), mod_min_kmer_obs (30), mod_fisher_lag (0),
# mod_max_obs_per_kmer (20000), mod_per_read (False).

# Alignment filter: mapped primary alignments at or above a mapping quality
# (unmapped, secondary and supplementary are always removed). Default 20; set with
#   snakemake --config filter_mapq=0     # keep every mapped primary alignment
# It applies to all samples and reruns everything downstream of the filter.

# Pod5 / signal analysis settings
# Uncomment and set when using pod5 raw data as input instead of FASTQ/BAM.
# Place pod5 files in raw_data/{SampleName}/ (directory, not file).
# Dorado model. Default is a pinned model with CpG 5mC/5hmC calling enabled:
#   dna_r10.4.1_e8.2_400bps_sup@v5.2.0_5mCG_5hmCG@v2
# The built-in 5mCG_5hmCG is what makes dorado emit MM/ML modification tags;
# without it no methylation analysis is possible and basecalling must be redone.
# Note the UNDERSCORE: a modification after a comma only works with the shorthand
# ('sup,5mCG_5hmCG'), not with a full model name. This exact name does NOT
# auto-select chemistry from pod5 metadata — use 'sup,5mCG_5hmCG' for
# auto-selection, or 'sup' for no modification calling.
#^dorado-model	dna_r10.4.1_e8.2_400bps_sup@v5.2.0_5mCG_5hmCG@v2
